.git
# Patterns are anchored at the context root, so a bare `node_modules` skips
# only the root one. web/node_modules and scaffolder/node_modules count too.
**/node_modules
output
batch/logs
batch/batch-state.tsv
batch/batch-input.tsv
batch/tracker-additions
jds/*
!jds/.gitkeep
reports/*.md
.env
.update-dismissed
.update-lock
*.log
.DS_Store
writing-samples

# User Layer (DATA_CONTRACT.md). The Dockerfile copies only package.json and
# the project is bind-mounted at runtime, so none of this belongs in the
# build context, which is sent to the Docker daemon on every build.
cv.md
article-digest.md
voice-dna.md
portals.yml
config/profile.yml
config/plugins.yml
config/cv-facts.json
config/local-paths.txt
data
documents
interview-prep
modes/_profile.md
modes/_custom.md
modes/_brief.md
.career-ops-web
plugins.local

# Build output
web/.next
dashboard/career-dashboard
dashboard/career-dashboard.exe
